(VAR-58: exactly one character between single quotes is a character literal,
 not an identifier, which is why single-character quoted identifiers do not
 exist. The declaration below fails because 'x' has already become the
 integer 120 by the time a name is wanted — the parser's own message says
 so: 120 is the ASCII code of x, so the single-quoted token was lexed as a
 character literal. (Compile-error claim: not assertable from a runtime leaf.)
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox VAR-58.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Expected a name, got IntegerLiteral(120)
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a number called 'x' is 5.
Print 'x'.
